    }
  }
)

#set table(style = "ReviewTable")

# Tables And Media Review

This page compares markdown tables, directive tables, captions, figures, and relative image loading. The markdown tables should use natural content width unless a width is explicitly supplied.

## Markdown Table

| Phase | Owner | Status | Budget |
| --- | --- | :---: | ---: |
| Parser fixtures | Engineering | Complete | $4,200 |
| PDF emitter | Engineering | In review | $6,800 |
| Visual QA | Design | Scheduled | $1,450 |
| Documentation | Product | Drafting | $950 |

## Explicit Wide Table

#table(width = pt(450), alignment = "center")[
  #row[
    #cell[Area]
    #cell[PDF]
    #cell[Word]
  ]
  #row[
    #cell[Divider]
    #cell[Drawn full text width]
    #cell[Styled paragraph border]
  ]
  #row[
    #cell[Markdown table]
    #cell[Natural width by default]
    #cell[Natural width by default]
  ]
]

#figure(kind = "image", alignment = "center", numbering = { enabled = true, label = "Figure" })[
  #image("assets/mote-logo.png", width = pt(120), alt = "Mote logo", border = { color = "#cbd5e1", width = pt(1) })
  #caption[Relative images should resolve from the source file in both backends.]
]

#break()

## Continuation Page

The second page provides more table rows to test page flow around table-heavy content. A single tall cell does not need to split perfectly yet, but ordinary rows should continue cleanly.

| Item | Owner | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Markdown heading | Parser | Lowers to a heading element. |
| Markdown paragraph | Parser | Lowers to a paragraph element. |
| Markdown divider | Parser | Lowers to a divider element. |
| Markdown table | Parser | Lowers to table, row, and cell elements. |
| Image directive | Emitter | Uses asset loading and relative path resolution. |
| Caption directive | Emitter | Uses local sequence counters where supported. |
| Header directive | Layout | Repeats page-level content. |
| Footer directive | Layout | Repeats page-level content. |
| Columns directive | Layout | Changes section-local text flow. |

The continuation page should look like a normal page, not a special case. The image on the first page should not disturb the table flow that follows.
